Wazuh API Examples

This page contains **real, working** Wazuh API examples using `curl`. All examples assume:

- You have API access enabled on your Wazuh manager.
- You know the API user and password (or already have a token).
- You have `jq` installed for pretty-printing JSON.

> Replace `https://your-wazuh-manager:55000`, `wazuh`, and `wazuh-password` with your real values.

---

1. Authenticate and get a JWT token

```bash
# Wazuh API URL and credentials
WAZUH_API="https://your-wazuh-manager:55000"
USER="wazuh"
PASSWORD="wazuh-password"

Get JWT token
TOKEN=$(curl -sku "$USER:$PASSWORD" -X GET \
  "$WAZUH_API/security/user/authenticate" | jq -r '.data.token')

echo "Token: $TOKEN"
```

---

2. List all agents

```bash
curl -k -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  "$WAZUH_API/agents" | jq
```

---

3. Get agent details by ID

```bash
AGENT_ID="001"  # change to your agent ID

curl -k -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  "$WAZUH_API/agents/$AGENT_ID" | jq
```

---

4. Get only **active** agents

```bash
curl -k -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  "$WAZUH_API/agents?status=active" | jq
```

