## 18. Example: simple Bash wrapper script

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash

WAZUH_API="https://your-wazuh-manager:55000"
USER="wazuh"
PASSWORD="wazuh-password"

get_token() {
  TOKEN=$(curl -sku "$USER:$PASSWORD" -X GET \
    "$WAZUH_API/security/user/authenticate" | jq -r '.data.token')
}

list_agents() {
  curl -k -X GET \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
    "$WAZUH_API/agents" | jq
}

get_token
list_agents
```

---

### Notes

- Use `-k` only for testing with self-signed certificates; configure proper TLS in production.
- Do **not** hard-code real passwords or tokens into scripts that are committed to Git.
- For production, prefer environment variables, secrets managers, or CI/CD secrets over plaintext credentials.
